                {
                  "mapping_justification": "Narrower than this entry's MONDO:0100244 term. MONDO's \"PNH2\" (OMIM #615399) is the PIGT-related form. It is still a somatically driven clonal hematopoietic stem cell disease, not an inherited non-clonal one: what distinguishes it from the PIGA disease this entry models is the germline *first* hit \u2014 a hypomorphic PIGT allele unmasked by a somatic second hit in the clone \u2014 rather than the absence of a somatic event. MONDO's own synonym for the term is \"paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria 2, autosomal dominant, somatic mutation\". The gene and the order of hits differ; the clonal somatic mechanism does not. Not yet curated here in genetic or pathophysiology detail, so recorded at disease level with `skos:narrowMatch` pending a dedicated curation pass.",
